DirkuLator 0.70rc: the design of Eglantine pull request 900 (Fix/oot texture handle remap), for our tree. Adds
Tegra::Texture::TextureHeaderIndex and UsesHeaderByteOffsetHandles. Some Switch 2 bindless handles (Switch Sports Resort's
scenery) hold the texture header's byte offset in the pool (index * 32) where the handle normally has the index; that reading
is switched on only for that title (program id 0x0400000000000849) and only on the native-tiling path, and only when the plain
index lies past the pool and the offset lands inside it. Ocarina of Time has an out-of-range handle (0xbe000) that must stay
out of range: it reads as no texture. Both places that turn a handle into a header index use it: the shader compile read
(GenericEnvironment::ReadTextureInfo, which no longer reads past the end of the table, it returns an empty header) and the
texture cache (VisitImageView). Compile-time checks in texture.h.

